the mystery of cake.

00:09:19.324 --> 00:09:21.360
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:22.694
-So, I don't know.
Is that good?

00:09:22.694 --> 00:09:25.764
-I think the problem is, like,
if you also were high,

00:09:25.764 --> 00:09:27.966
a little bit drunk,
and on sizzurp, that cake show,

00:09:27.966 --> 00:09:29.702
you might be like -- that might
be right up your alley.

00:09:29.702 --> 00:09:31.203
[ Laughter ]

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:32.971
-That's why it's so popular.
-That's the problem.

00:09:32.971 --> 00:09:34.707
You, like, made a film
at the wrong time.

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:37.309
It came out at the wrong time.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.309 --> 00:09:39.611
You also have made,
over the course of your career,

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:40.879
some fantastic documentaries,

00:09:40.879 --> 00:09:42.181
and I'm really excited
about this.

00:09:42.181 --> 00:09:46.185
You have a documentary for HBO
about George Carlin.

00:09:46.185 --> 00:09:48.421
-Yes, in May it's coming out.

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:49.788
-You know,
he's a fantastic comedian.

00:09:49.788 --> 00:09:51.857
I feel like, obviously,
as time passes,

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:54.393
less and less people are maybe
familiar with his work.

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:57.195
You knew his work a great deal
when he was alive.

00:09:57.195 --> 00:09:59.465
And what is one of the things
you found,

00:09:59.465 --> 00:10:01.700
going back
and looking at his material?

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.803
-Well, what was weird is,
anytime something happens

00:10:03.803 --> 00:10:05.604
in the world,
no matter what it is,

00:10:05.604 --> 00:10:09.575
he trends because he has the
best stand-up bit on the topic.

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:11.376
-A modern topic.
-Anything.

00:10:11.376 --> 00:10:14.280
Viruses, big pharma, abortion,
the government.

00:10:14.280 --> 00:10:15.715
You know, like, everything,
he's got the bit,

00:10:15.715 --> 00:10:17.016
and it just starts trending.

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:20.319
And I only saw him once.
He was at Igby's in L.A.,

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:21.854
working on a new set,
and he would sit there and,

00:10:21.854 --> 00:10:24.456
like, memorize it like a play.

00:10:24.456 --> 00:10:25.757
All I remember,
and I don't remember the jokes,

00:10:25.757 --> 00:10:27.359
is he said to the audience,
"There are certain things

00:10:27.359 --> 00:10:30.195
you're not allowed
to make jokes about,

00:10:30.195 --> 00:10:32.298
and that's
what I'm going to do right now."

00:10:32.298 --> 00:10:34.733
[ Laughter ]
And just went at --

00:10:34.733 --> 00:10:38.137
whatever you could imagine
as the worst topic,

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:40.839
he did that night.
-Being as familiar as you were

00:10:40.839 --> 00:10:42.274
with his work,
was it also an education

00:10:42.274 --> 00:10:45.144
to go back to the old stuff?
-Oh, yeah, because, you know,

00:10:45.144 --> 00:10:48.180
he was kind of corny
in the '60s,

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:50.749
and then, suddenly, he's like,
"I want to be edgy."

00:10:50.749 --> 00:10:53.185
And then he grew a beard,
and he became the edgiest guy.

00:10:53.185 --> 00:10:55.220
And then he got kind of
soft again and did, like,

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.521
"Place for my Stuff."

00:10:56.521 --> 00:10:59.058
And then he saw Sam Kinison --
he saw Sam Kinison,

00:10:59.058 --> 00:11:01.627
and he thought, "I don't want to
be soft compared to this guy."

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:03.895
And then he tried to, like,
outdo Sam Kinison

00:11:03.895 --> 00:11:05.697
for the rest of his career.
-That's fantastic.

00:11:05.697 --> 00:11:06.865
I can't wait to see that.

00:11:06.865 --> 00:11:07.933
And it's always so great
to see you.

00:11:07.933 --> 00:11:09.401
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:11:09.401 --> 00:11:10.503
-Great to see ya.
-You guys, Judd Apatow,

00:11:10.503 --> 00:11:12.371
"The Bubble,"
streaming on Netflix.

00:11:12.371 --> 00:11:13.906
"Sicker in the Head"
is available now.

